      "sourceTextSha256": "167c0cd9e9b944713b8889fd404dd900d1a43d8fef2f713105b9bf6e335ded33",
      "text": "Today you’ll visit two archaeological sites.\n\nTulum was a Maya port and trading centre, built on a cliff above the Caribbean Sea. Goods passed through the city between the coast and inland Yucatán. The archaeological site is relatively small, with a surviving defensive wall, temples, murals and bas-reliefs.\n\nNext you’ll travel to Cobá, one of the oldest cities of the Maya civilisation. At its height, it covered about 50 km² and was an important political, commercial and religious centre in the eastern Yucatán Peninsula.\n\nYou’ll see surviving white roads known as sacbé, courts for the Maya ball game pok-ta-pok and tall pyramids. The itinerary includes a climb up Nohoch Mul, a 42-metre pyramid.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-work-e805e5042bc7",
        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol"
      }
    },
